A '''beetroot'''{{fn|Also known as a '''beet''' in [[Language#Differences between English variants|Canadian English]].}} is a [[food]] and [[dye]] ingredient.

== Obtaining ==
=== Farming ===
Beetroots are obtained from harvesting a fully-grown beetroot crop, which drops 1 beetroot {{in|je}} or 1 to 2 beetroots {{in|be}} and 1 to 4 beetroot seeds ({{frac|2|5|7}} per crop harvested on average). If a crop is harvested before it is fully grown, it just drops one seed. Harvesting with a [[Fortune]]-enchanted tool increases the number of seeds dropped but does not increase the yield of beetroots.

== Usage ==
=== Food ===
{{see also|Tutorial:Hunger management|title1=Hunger management}}
A beetroot can be eaten to restore {{hunger|1}} [[hunger]] and 1.2 hunger [[Hunger#Mechanics|saturation]]. Six beetroots can be crafted into [[beetroot soup]], which restores six times the hunger and saturation of a single beetroot.

=== Crafting ingredient ===
{{crafting usage}}

=== Breeding ===
Beetroots can be used to breed and attract [[pig]]s.

[[Villager]]s can pick up beetroot items to become willing, allowing them to [[Breeding|breed]]. Villagers need 12 beetroots before they can breed.

=== Composting ===
Placing a beetroot into a [[composter]] has a 65% chance of raising the compost level by 1.

